# The repository is LF — in the index and in the working tree. See docs/DECISIONS.md D95.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect a binary by content, so one added later is left alone.
# `eol=lf` is the half that does the work, and it is NOT redundant with `text=auto`: measured against a
# clone with `core.autocrlf=true`, `text=auto` alone checks out CRLF and this line checks out LF. The
# attribute beats the config — which is the point, since the config is untracked and differs per clone.

* text=auto eol=lf
